<title>USA: Woodhead's DeWinter to add chairman title.</title>
<headline>Woodhead's DeWinter to add chairman title.</headline>
<dateline>BUFFALO GROVE, Ill. 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Woodhead Industries Inc said Friday that in addition to his responsibilities as president and chief executive officer, C. Mark DeWinter will become chairman of the company.</p>
<p>DeWinter succeeds Alan Reed, who retired, concluding a 38-year career with Woodhead, which develops and manufactures specialty electrical devices and fiber optic cable assemblies, among other products.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
